From 4165284da888c7155f1a25a273bd0d0c2d996526 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:32:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] fix(core): reject pods_run ports outside 1-65535

pods_run converted its port argument to int32 with no range check.
A negative port silently skipped the Service (the Pod was created, the
call succeeded), and values of 2^31 and above wrapped: 4294967376
became a Service on port 80. The API refuses both values when they
reach it as a Service port.

The port is now checked as an int64, before the conversion: values
below 0 or above 65535 are refused with an error and nothing is
created. No port, or 0, still exposes nothing. The fractional-value
truncation (8080.9 becomes 8080) is the separate issue #1584 and is
not changed here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit a37eb05a44fe7de621f866d27ce8fdb399875282)
